# Cloudflare Pages rewrite rules.
#
# Routing left the hash behind: the marketing pages needed addresses people can
# read and share (`/huong-dan`, `/co-gi-moi/0.7.1`) and the game needed to live
# at `/play`. None of those are files on disk, so a cold load of one — a
# bookmark, a shared link, a refresh — asks Cloudflare for a path it does not
# have and gets the 404 page.
#
# `200` rather than `301`: the address stays what the visitor typed, and the
# router reads it once React is up. A redirect would rewrite every deep link to
# `/` and lose the destination.
#
# Real files always win over this rule, so `/icon.svg`, `/sfx/move.mp3`,
# `/assets/*` and the rest are still served as themselves.

# Old hash-era links, kept working. `/#/play` cannot be matched here — the
# fragment never reaches the server — so that one is handled in `src/main.tsx`.
/about        /gioi-thieu   301
/changelog    /co-gi-moi    301
/changelog/*  /co-gi-moi/:splat  301

/*  /index.html  200
